    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0841" n="829" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg829"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harry L. Hopkins, Adviser and Assistant to the
                        President, to the Chairman of the Council of People’s Commissars of the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stalin</hi>)<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d629-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rochester, Minnesota</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-13">April 13, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret to Premier Stalin from Harry Hopkins.</p>
                <p>I heard your message broadcast to the American people today<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d629-f2"/> but I want you to know that I feel that Russia has lost
                    her greatest friend in America. The President was ever deeply impressed by your
                    determination and confidence that the Nazi tyrants of the world will be driven
                    from power forever.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry Hopkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d629-f1" n="41" type="source" xml:id="d629-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram obtained from the Franklin D. Roosevelt Library, Hyde Park, N.Y.
                    On this day Mr. Hopkins was a patient at St. Mary’s Hospital in Rochester,
                    Minnesota.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d629-f2" n="42" xml:id="d629-f2-content">
                <p>For Marshal Stalin’s message to Mrs. Roosevelt, broadcast by Moscow radio on
                    April 13, see the <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>, April 13, 1945,
                    p. 10, col. 7.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
